WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.749 --> 00:00:17.836
One day Robin Hood was on a road near Sherwood Forest.

2
00:00:18.637 --> 00:00:21.518
Little John and two more men walked with him.

3
00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:25.180
They were Arthur of Bland and Will Scarlet.

4
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.941
"I'm hungry!"

5
00:00:28.382 --> 00:00:29.022
said Robin.

6
00:00:29.042 --> 00:00:32.384
"I'd like a good loaf of bread and some cheese."

7
00:00:33.272 --> 00:00:35.873
"I know an inn nearby," said Arthur.

8
00:00:35.893 --> 00:00:37.553
"I'll buy us lunch."

9
00:00:42.215 --> 00:00:44.935
He soon returned with some bread and cheese.

10
00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:48.716
The four men sat behind a hedge and ate.

11
00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:51.457
"That was good."

12
00:00:51.957 --> 00:00:53.057
Little John sighed.

13
00:00:53.077 --> 00:00:56.238
"Yes, it was," Robin agreed.

14
00:00:56.258 --> 00:00:58.559
"Let's finish our meal with some music.

15
00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:00.740
Sing for us, Will!"

16
00:01:03.992 --> 00:01:06.713
First, Will sang and then Arthur sang.

17
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:12.494
"Now it's your turn, Little John," said Robin.

18
00:01:12.514 --> 00:01:17.416
"I'm not much of a singer," Little John said modestly.

19
00:01:17.436 --> 00:01:21.037
"I spoil most songs when I sing."

20
00:01:21.057 --> 00:01:23.277
"Come on!"

21
00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:24.998
The other men coaxed him.

22
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:28.138
Finally Little John began a tune.

23
00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:33.480
"Stop!" said Robin suddenly.

24
00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:36.270
"Who's that man coming down the road?"

25
00:01:36.851 --> 00:01:37.812
The other men looked.

26
00:01:38.512 --> 00:01:41.134
"He's just a miller," said Little John.

27
00:01:41.154 --> 00:01:45.298
"He's harmless—there was no reason for me to stop singing."

28
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.502
All four men kept their eyes on the miller.

29
00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:57.129
The young man's clothes were covered with flour, and he carried a heavy sack over his shoulder.

30
00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:00.572
A thick staff rested on top of the sack.

31
00:02:01.456 --> 00:02:05.038
His hair and beard were blond and his cheeks were flushed.

32
00:02:05.978 --> 00:02:08.739
"He looks like a good, honest man," said Robin.

33
00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:10.520
"Let's play a trick on him.

34
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.921
We'll act like thieves and pretend to rob him.

35
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:16.682
Then we'll take him to the forest for a feast.

36
00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.743
But we won't steal his money.

37
00:02:19.303 --> 00:02:23.445
For every coin in his wallet, we'll give him 25 more."

38
00:02:23.465 --> 00:02:27.687
"That sounds like a good plan," said Arthur.

39
00:02:28.407 --> 00:02:30.048
Will's eyes twinkled merrily.

40
00:02:31.316 --> 00:02:32.356
"It sounds like fun!"

41
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:33.177
he said.

42
00:02:33.637 --> 00:02:35.657
Little John was frowning slightly.

43
00:02:35.677 --> 00:02:42.019
"I'm very tired," he complained, "and my bones ache.

44
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.480
I don't want to get into a fight with this fellow."

45
00:02:46.781 --> 00:02:48.221
Robin laughed at him.

46
00:02:48.241 --> 00:02:51.102
"There are four of us and he's alone.

47
00:02:51.902 --> 00:02:53.883
He has no prayer against us."

48
00:02:54.863 --> 00:02:56.844
The miller was now across the road.

49
00:02:57.856 --> 00:03:01.378
The four men jumped out and surrounded the frightened man.

50
00:03:01.398 --> 00:03:06.860
"Your sack looks heavy," said Robin.

51
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.981
"Do you need help carrying it?"

52
00:03:09.001 --> 00:03:10.581
"Who are you?"

53
00:03:10.961 --> 00:03:11.742
growled the miller.

54
00:03:12.382 --> 00:03:16.944
His voice was deep and gruff, and he clearly didn't trust these strangers.

55
00:03:16.964 --> 00:03:18.925
"We're just four helpful men."

56
00:03:19.305 --> 00:03:20.145
Robin smiled.

57
00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:22.226
"Are you sure we can't help you?"

58
00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:24.707
"No thanks," said the miller.

59
00:03:24.727 --> 00:03:26.308
"My sack's not heavy.

60
00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:28.289
There's only flour inside."

61
00:03:28.309 --> 00:03:31.471
"I have a good nose for smelling money.

62
00:03:32.172 --> 00:03:35.734
I think your sack holds some heavy coins," said Robin.

63
00:03:35.754 --> 00:03:37.956
"I don't have any money with me.

64
00:03:38.436 --> 00:03:40.157
And let me warn you," said the miller.

65
00:03:40.177 --> 00:03:42.499
"You're near Robin Hood's home.

66
00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:46.922
If he hears you robbed an honest man, you'll be in trouble."

67
00:03:49.563 --> 00:03:51.064
"I'm not afraid of Robin Hood!"

68
00:03:51.625 --> 00:03:53.486
said Robin, trying not to laugh.

69
00:03:53.506 --> 00:03:56.188
"Arthur, empty this man's sack.

70
00:03:57.172 --> 00:03:59.093
I'm sure we'll find some money in there."

71
00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:01.014
"No, no!

72
00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:02.455
Don't ruin my flour!"

73
00:04:02.936 --> 00:04:03.696
cried the miller.

74
00:04:03.716 --> 00:04:05.477
"I'll get the money for you."

75
00:04:06.158 --> 00:04:08.719
He opened the sack and dug into the flour.

76
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.722
Robin and his men gathered around the miller and leaned eagerly toward his sack.

77
00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:18.705
Suddenly the miller reached up—and threw flour in their faces.

78
00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.908
Arthur's mouth had been wide open.

79
00:04:23.676 --> 00:04:27.277
Now poor Arthur coughed so hard, he started choking!

80
00:04:28.117 --> 00:04:30.858
The miller threw more and more flour at them.

81
00:04:31.518 --> 00:04:35.019
Their hair and beards and clothes were as white as snow.

82
00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.041
Robin and his men rubbed their eyes—none of them could see!

83
00:04:40.921 --> 00:04:44.282
Then the miller grabbed his staff and started beating them.

84
00:04:45.723 --> 00:04:46.963
"Stop! Stop!"

85
00:04:47.483 --> 00:04:48.183
cried Robin.

86
00:04:48.203 --> 00:04:49.884
"I'm Robin Hood!"

87
00:04:50.776 --> 00:04:51.796
"Don't lie to me!"

88
00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.877
The miller smacked Robin again.

89
00:04:53.897 --> 00:04:56.859
"Robin Hood would never rob an honest man."

90
00:04:57.679 --> 00:05:00.080
Robin and his men kept rubbing their eyes.

91
00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.442
Little John and Will were now coughing too.

92
00:05:05.262 --> 00:05:09.104
The miller kept throwing flour and hitting everyone with his staff.

93
00:05:10.324 --> 00:05:12.165
Finally Robin found his horn.

94
00:05:12.765 --> 00:05:15.826
He blew three times and a group of his men appeared.

95
00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.428
One of the men grabbed the miller.

96
00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.208
"What should we do with him, Robin?"

97
00:05:21.228 --> 00:05:24.129
"Robin?" the miller said weakly.

98
00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:26.510
"You're really Robin Hood?"

99
00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.230
"That's right!"

100
00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.691
Robin's men said in one voice.

101
00:05:30.711 --> 00:05:31.891
"Oh no."

102
00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.472
The miller looked around in fear.

103
00:05:34.492 --> 00:05:38.493
"You put up quite a fight," said Robin.

104
00:05:38.513 --> 00:05:40.534
"We weren't going to rob you.

105
00:05:41.114 --> 00:05:43.634
In fact, we were going to give you money.

106
00:05:44.275 --> 00:05:45.295
What's your name, Miller?"

107
00:05:45.315 --> 00:05:51.209
"Midge." "Well, Midge," said Robin, "would you like to join our band?"

108
00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.330
Midge looked embarrassed.

109
00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:56.012
"Will you forgive me for attacking you?"

110
00:05:56.372 --> 00:05:56.933
he asked.

111
00:05:58.034 --> 00:05:59.795
"Of course," said Robin.

112
00:05:59.815 --> 00:06:02.977
"We always enjoy a good fight."

113
00:06:04.478 --> 00:06:05.338
Midge grinned.

114
00:06:05.358 --> 00:06:07.420
"Then I'll be happy to join you!"
